meta {
  name: Get College Section
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/colleges/{{collegeId}}/section/{{sectionName}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

vars:pre-request {
  sectionName: college_overview
}

docs {
  Returns the content of a single college-level static tab by its section ID.

  Path params:
  - collegeId: College UUID (set via list-colleges or get-by-id scripts)
  - sectionName: One of the static tab IDs returned in the `tabs` array from Get College By Id

  Supported sectionName values (college-level static tabs only):
  college_overview, course_info, placements, fees,
  financial_aid, student_housing, exam_policy, faculty, review, commute,
  library, clubs_associations, student_code_of_conduct, happenings,
  institutions_across_world, alliance, demo_graphics

  Note: admission_policy is course-level only (see Get Course Tab /
  Get Course Eligibility Criteria) — not a valid college-level sectionName.

  Response:
  {
    "sectionName": "college_overview",
    "sectionId": "college_overview",
    "sectionKey": "college_overview",
    "data": { ... section content ... }
  }

  Returns 404 if the section does not exist or is disabled for this college.

  ## college_overview — campus_ambassadors (live, computed)
  The `campus_ambassadors` field inside `college_overview` is always
  computed live from the blink_users table (role: campus_ambassador,
  status: active for this college). Any static value saved in
  profileSections for this key is replaced by the live data.

  Shape of each ambassador object:
  {
    "name": string,          // blinkUser.fullName
    "image": string,         // blinkUser.avatarUrl ?? ""
    "state": string,         // blinkUser.profileMetadata.state ?? ""
    "course": string,        // blinkUser.profileMetadata.course ?? ""
    "district": string,      // blinkUser.profileMetadata.district ?? ""
    "message_link": string   // blinkUser.profileMetadata.message_link ?? ""
  }

  Table: blink_users (role = campus_ambassador, status = active)

  ## commute (live, computed — profileSections.commute is ignored)
  Built entirely from the college-admin Commute page data (active routes,
  their stops and active buses). 404 when the college has no active routes;
  the `commute` tab in Get College By Id/Slug only appears when it has one.

  {
    "data": {
      "id": "commute", "tab": "commute", "title": "Commute",
      "route_count": number,
      "pickup_points": string[],          // unique pickup stop names
      "routes": [
        {
          "route_name", "via",             // route name / description
          "pickup_point",                  // first pickup stop
          "status": "VERIFIED" | "UNVERIFIED",
          "timings": [{ "label": "Morning" | "Evening", "time": "7:30 AM" }],
          "transport_fee": { "amount": "₹1,500" | "From ₹1,200" | "Free", "payment_structure": "month" },
          "bus_information": { "registration_number", "seats", "model" },  // first bus
          "morning_pickup_points": [{ "point", "landmark", "time" }],
          "evening_dropoff_points": [{ "point", "landmark", "time" }]     // reverse stop order
        }
      ],
      "rules_and_code_of_conduct": {
        "title", "subtitle", "intro",
        "rules": [{ "title", "description" }]   // all routes' conduct policies, deduped by title
      }
    }
  }

  Table: commute_routes, commute_route_stops, commute_buses

  ## institutions_across_world (live, computed — not the stored static content)
  Like `commute`, this section is always computed live from the college's
  institution-group membership and overlays the stored profileSections
  content. If the college has no group, `group` is null and `institutions`
  is an empty array.

  {
    "data": {
      "id": "institutions_across_world",
      "title": "Institution Across the World",
      "enabled": true,
      "group": { "id", "name", "groupCode", "status" } | null,
      "institutions": [
        {
          "id", "name", "code", "slug", "logoUrl", "city", "state",
          "country": "India",
          "role", "joinedAt", "joinedVia",
          "selected": true,
          "departments": [
            {
              "id", "name",
              "programs_available": number,
              "expanded": boolean,
              "program_type_tabs": { "selected": string, "options": string[] },
              "courses": [
                { "id", "name", "duration", "mode", "fee": string | null, "currency": "INR" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
        // sibling group members (selected: false) only include
        // id/name/code/slug/logoUrl/city/state/country — role, joinedAt,
        // joinedVia are "" and departments is [] for every college other
        // than the one matching :collegeId in the URL.
      ]
    }
  }

  Note: "departments" groups the viewed college's active courses by
  Discipline (id/name = the Discipline row), not by the `Department`
  model — `Department` has no admin UI/API yet, while every course
  already has a disciplineId via the existing course form. Only
  disciplines with at least one active course appear.

  Table: institution_groups, institution_group_members, courses, disciplines, fee_structures
}
